<title>USA: Odyssey Partners dissolving $3 billion firm - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Odyssey Partners dissolving $3 billion firm - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private investment firm Odyssey Partners is dissolving due to the fact the $3 billion hedge fund has become too bulky to easily invest, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>Odyssey has already sold most of its holdings, the story said.</p>
<p>The fund also owns stakes in about 20 companies which partners in the firm said may take several years to liquidate, according to the story.</p>
